{
  "_readme": [
    "The corpus: one entry per word or phrase somebody has actually SEEN",
    "written in Avatarian. See CORPUS.md for why this exists and TODO.md",
    "items 20-24 for what is built on it.",
    "",
    "SPELLINGS ARE STORED IN IPA, not in the codes the sounds box shows.",
    "IPA is canonical and does not move; the ASCII codes are an input and",
    "display layer over it. That is exactly what let the codes be replaced",
    "wholesale in session 10 (TODO item 29, ARPAbet -> readable) without a",
    "single line of this file changing.",
    "",
    "A spelling is the FINISHED BLOCK STRUCTURE, flattened: read the blocks",
    "left to right, each one top slot then bottom slot. Nulls are written",
    "out, so the token count is always EVEN and re-pairing the list two at",
    "a time reproduces the blocks exactly. That is the whole trick that",
    "lets `appa` (three blocks where pairing predicts two) live in the same",
    "shape as every other entry.",
    "",
    "  appa   ɑ ∅ p ∅ ɑ ∅   ->  (ɑ,∅) (p,∅) (ɑ,∅)",
    "",
    "Write the generic null ∅. Which null is actually drawn is decided by",
    "its pairing partner (render.js `nullFor`), so recording ∅c would be",
    "recording an interpretation rather than the observation. B3 confirmed",
    "that rule against the art in session 10 and not one line here had to",
    "change, which is the point of keeping the two apart.",
    "",
    "`$` / `%` force a glyph's top / bottom orientation where the slot does",
    "not decide it. Only /s/ needs this today.",
    "",
    "Edit this file, or use the workbench: python3 tools/corpus_server.py",
    "Then run: python3 tools/build_corpus.py"
  ],
